<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>FL2026 exam 38</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; }
h1 { color: #C0392B; font-size: 20pt; }
h2 { color: #1F618D; font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 24px; }
.qtext { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
.opt { margin: 4px 0 4px 20px; }
.correct { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedwrong { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedright { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.explain { background: #F4F6F6; padding: 8px; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }
.video { margin-top:6px; }
img { max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; display:block; }
</style></head><body><h1>FL2026 EXAM 38 - Ket qua &amp; giai thich</h1><p><b>Ho ten:</b> Hang Tran<br/><b>Ket qua:</b> 8/31<br/><b>Thoi gian lam bai:</b> 01 phút 14 giây<br/><b>Nop bai:</b> 2026-08-03T07:31:33.513Z</p><hr/><h2>Cau hoi 1</h2><div class="qtext">How many test cases are needed minimum to achieve 100 % statement coverage? if ((temperature &lt; 0) or (temperature &gt; 100)) { alert ("DANGER"); if ((speed &gt; 100) and (load &lt;= 50)) { speed = 50; } } else { check = false; }</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 1 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. 2 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. 3</div><div class="opt ">d. 4</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3 phần whitebox test và phải vẽ đc sơ đồ flow</div><h2>Cau hoi 2</h2><div class="qtext">A daily radiation recorder for plants produces a sunshine score based on a combination of the number of hours a plant is exposed to the sun (below 2 hours, 2 to 4 hours, 4 to 6 hours, 6 to 8 hours, above 8 hours) and the average intensity of the sunshine (very low, low, medium, high). Given the following test cases ( image) What is the minimum number of additional test cases that are needed to ensure full coverage of ALL VALID INPUT equivalence partitions?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 1 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 2</div><div class="opt correct">c. 3 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 4</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.2.1 phần EP, họ hỏi số TC cần thêm vào để bao phủ hết các EP, vẽ ra các EP rồi map với cái bảng TC họ đã cho xem EP nào đã đc test, tính các EP còn lại để ra đc TC</div><h2>Cau hoi 3</h2><div class="qtext">Which work product can be used by an agile team to show the amount of work that has been completed and the amount of total work remaining for a given iteration?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Acceptance criteria [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Defect report</div><div class="opt ">c. Test completion report</div><div class="opt correct">d. Burndown chart [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.4 cái này là kiến thức của AGile, cái để theo dõi tiến độ của task công việc, bao nhiêu đã complete và bao nhiêu remaining là cái burndown chart. lưu ý burn down chart có thể ko nằm trong test report vì đây là biểu đồ dùng quản lý cả dự án Agile</div><h2>Cau hoi 4</h2><div class="qtext">Which TWO of the review types below are the BEST fitted (most adequate) options to choose for reviewing safety critical components in a software project?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Informal review. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">b. Management review. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">c. Inspection [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Walkthrough.</div><div class="opt correct">e. Technical Review. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2 Review types, vì đây là dự án safety critical nên nó cần có hình thức review cao nhất formal nhất để thực hiện</div><h2>Cau hoi 5</h2><div class="qtext">Which of following statement does NOT correctly describe a valid approach to Component testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Functional testing of the component in isolation. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Structure-based testing of the code without recording incidents.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Functional testing of the interfaces between modules. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Automated tests that are run until the component passes.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2 Test levels. Các bạn loại đi đáp án C ko phải của component test vì interfaces between modules là của integration test</div><h2>Cau hoi 6</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is an advantage of the whole team approach?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Any person in the team with the right skills can perform any task [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Tasks are assigned to specific team members who will own that task until completion</div><div class="opt ">c. Testers have clear ownership of quality and this eliminates confusion and overlap</div><div class="opt ">d. Business representatives are not included in the team so they can supply independent assessment during UAT</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.5 phần Whole team approach, nhớ là mọi member đều có khả năng thực hiện any task, mọi người đều có trách nhiệm như nhau, câu D nó nói BA ko phải là thành viên của team là sai nhé,</div><h2>Cau hoi 7</h2><div class="qtext">A top-down development strategy affects which level of testing most?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Component testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Integration testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. System testing</div><div class="opt ">d. User acceptance testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2 test level, bạn nhớ xem top-down là chiến lược tích hợp của integration level</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">To test a function, the programmer has to write a.................. which calls the function to be tested and passes it test data:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Stub [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Driver [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Proxy</div><div class="opt ">d. None of the above</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2 test level phần component test, bạn vẽ ra cái sơ đồ driver --&gt; module A--&gt; stubs sau đó nhớ lại là cái gì pass test data cho module A chính là driver, còn stub chỉ ghi kết quả ra thôi</div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">Which tool would typically be used by developers?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Comparator tool [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Modelling tool [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Test execution tool</div><div class="opt ">d. Tool support for review</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 6.1 phần phân loại về tool, các tool đánh dấu chữ D ở cuối là dành cho developer</div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">According to the ISTQB syllabus, which of the following is a key benefit of early feedback in Agile project?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Increasing the total number of test cases required for the system. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Reducing the overall cost of quality by finding defects when they are easier and cheaper to fix. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Moving the responsibility of quality from the testers to the Product Owner.</div><div class="opt ">d. Providing a formal sign-off for each individual developer's code.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2.1 Early feedback. Lợi ích của feedback sớm bạn nhớ lại câu thần chú phần tips ở đầu chương 1, feedback sớm cũng giống review sớm: giảm cost</div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">In Agile software development, what is the primary purpose of establishing short feedback loops?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. To ensure that the project manager can micro-manage the daily tasks of the developers and testers. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. To minimize the time between the introduction of a defect and its discovery, thereby reducing technical debt. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. To replace the need for comprehensive documentation with frequent verbal updates.</div><div class="opt ">d. To provide a justification for increasing the number of automated test scripts in every iteration.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2.1, cái short feedback loops là các vòng lặp của phản hồi ngắn hay cũng chính là phản hồi sớm, nên nó có benefit là giống review sớm: Giảm thời gian</div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">Incident reports (or Defect reports) are test artifacts primarily associated with which part of the software development/testing life cycle?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Requirement Specification [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test Design and Test Implementation</div><div class="opt correct">c. Test Design and Test Execution [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Maintenance and Retirement</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.4 sản phầm Defect Report là của test activities nào ta chọn đc Execution</div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">How does Continuous Integration (CI) primarily contribute to software quality in an Agile project?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. By ensuring that the system is 100% free of defects before any manual testing begins. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. By providing early detection of integration errors and regressions through automated builds and tests. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. By shifting the entire responsibility of quality from the testers to the build automation tools.</div><div class="opt ">d. By eliminating the need for developers to perform any form of unit testing before committing code.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1.4 phần Devops đó, đọc kỹ các key word để chọn vì CI/CD là 1 phần của Devops mà, nên chọn B vì early detection lỗi tích hợp và automated cho regression test là 2 ý của Devops</div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">A tester participates in a technical discussion about the system's architecture and structure-based design. During an early prototype review, the tester performs a quick check on a search field and notices that the search results are significantly delayed, causing the screen to hang. By identifying this performance-related issue before the full implementation, the tester is fulfilling which role/activity in the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Impact Analysis [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Static Testing</div><div class="opt correct">c. Dynamic Testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Test Management</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.1.3. Kịch bản rất dài và dễ đánh lừa vì họ nói là tham gia vào review Architecture nhưng tester phải chạy prototype thì phát hiện ra perfomance issues, mà lỗi này phải do dynamic tìm ra, xem kỹ bảng so sánh lỗi của static và dynamic</div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">A smart thermostat system is designed to trigger different modes based on the ambient temperature: Cooling Mode: below 10°C. Eco Mode: from 10°C to 20°C (inclusive). Heating Mode: above 20°C. Using 2-point Boundary Value Analysis, which of the following sets of temperatures represents the minimum number of test cases to check the boundaries between the modes?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. 9, 10, 20, 21 [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. 5, 10, 20, 22</div><div class="opt ">c. 10, 11, 19, 20</div><div class="opt ">d. 5, 15, 25</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.1 EP</div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">In Exploratory Testing (ET), what is the primary benefit of using a Test Charter?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. It provides a detailed, step-by-step script that the tester must follow to ensure 100% test coverage. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. It acts as a formal contract that prevents the Product Owner from changing the requirements during the testing session.</div><div class="opt correct">c. It provides a clear focus and scope for the testing session without restricting the tester's ability to explore the system. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. It eliminates the need for any final test summary report by documenting all defects in real-time.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.4.2 ET. Test Charter là các guideline hướng dẫn cho việc test, nó ko có tt chi tiết của A (loại A), nó ko triệt tiêu nhu cầu về test summary report nên loại D,</div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">Programmers often write and execute unit tests against code which they have written. During this self-testing activity, which of the following is a tester mindset that programmers should adopt to perform this unit testing effectively?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Good communication skills [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Code coverage</div><div class="opt ">c. Evaluating code defects</div><div class="opt correct">d. Attention to detail [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.5.4 bảng mindset của tester và dev. Ở đây họ bảo Dev tự làm unit test ( self-test) nên Dev ko cần kỹ năng communication, vậy Dev cần có Attention to detail là mind set của tester để làm tốt công việc của mình</div><h2>Cau hoi 18</h2><div class="qtext">A tester is tasked with verifying the functional correctness of a new insurance calculation module. The tester designs test cases based on the requirement specifications to ensure the output matches the expected mathematical results. Which category of test techniques is being applied?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Structure-based (White-box) techniques [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Specification-based (Black-box) techniques [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Experience-based techniques</div><div class="opt ">d. Defect-based techniques</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2 test type, chú ý vào từ test functional correctness thì cần dùng kỹ thuật gì, là Black box test rồi</div><h2>Cau hoi 19</h2><div class="qtext">Maintenance testing is triggered by changes to an operational system. Which of the following is NOT a typical reason for performing maintenance testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Testing the system after migration to a new hardware platform or operating system. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Testing the archiving of data when a product reaches its end-of-life (Retirement).</div><div class="opt correct">c. Testing a brand-new software application that has never been released to the production environment. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Testing a hotfix implemented to correct a critical defect in the production environment.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.3 trigger cho maintainance test thì A là migration có, B archiving of data ( chuyển đổi data khi hệ thống cho nghỉ end of life) có, D có hotfix nên chỉ có C là ko phải trigger vì phần mềm này never release.</div><h2>Cau hoi 20</h2><div class="qtext">A greenhouse control system regulates the heater based on the following temperature requirements: Invalid (Too Low): Below 0.0°C Valid (Normal range): 0.0°C to 30.0°C (inclusive) Invalid (Too High): Above 30.0°C Which of the following sets of temperature inputs provides the highest Equivalence Partitioning coverage with the minimum number of test cases?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. -5.0°C, 15.0°C, 35.0°C [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. 0.0°C, 10.0°C, 20.0°C, 30.0°C</div><div class="opt ">c. 5.0°C, 25.0°C</div><div class="opt ">d. -10.0°C, 0.0°C, 30.0°C, 40.0°C</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2 BVA</div><h2>Cau hoi 21</h2><div class="qtext">Which TWO of the following statements CORRECTLY describes a role of impact analysis in Maintenance Testing?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Impact analysis is used when deciding if a fix to a maintained system is worthwhile. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt selectedright">b. Impact analysis is used to identify how data should be migrated into the maintained system. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Impact analysis is used to decide which hot fixes are of most value to the user.</div><div class="opt ">d. Impact analysis is used to determine the effectiveness of new maintenance test cases.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.3 Maintainance test. Impact analysis giúp để ra quyết định xem hệ thống có nên sửa ko if a fix to a maintained system is worthwhile. Câu này chỉ có A đúng, nhưng đề thi thật yêu cầu chọn 2 đáp án thì có thể chọn tạm B vì nó còn tốt hơn C và D. C thì cái most values to user thì impact analysis ko đánh giá đc, D thì new maintainance test case ko thuộc phạm vi của impact analysis. B chọn thêm mặc dù hơi kiên cưỡng vì how data should be migrated là công việc của đội kỹ thuật, có lẽ họ hỏi impact analysis là hỏi cả test và đội kỹ thuật</div><h2>Cau hoi 22</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following BEST defines risk level?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Risk level is calculated by adding together the probabilities of all problem situations and the financial harm that results from them. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Risk level is estimated by multiplying the likelihood of a threat to the system by the chance that the threat will occur and will result in financial damage</div><div class="opt correct">c. Risk level is determined by a combination of the probability of an undesirable event and the expected impact of that event. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Risk level is the sum of all potential hazards to a system multiplied by the sum of all potential losses from that system.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.3 phần risk management và risk level = impact x likelihood</div><h2>Cau hoi 23</h2><div class="qtext">An organization is planning an AI transfer initiative to upgrade their testing tool suite by integrating Machine Learning (ML) and Deep Learning models. They categorize the target AI-driven features into distinct engineering capabilities: Test Automation, Testing Techniques, Quality Characteristics, and Code Quality. Which of the following groups correctly aligns an AI-driven test capability with its corresponding practical application?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Auto GUI (Testing Technique), Black box (Test Automation), Security (Quality Characteristic), Code format (Code Quality) [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Auto GUI (Test Automation), Black box (Testing Technique), Security (Quality Characteristic), Performance (Quality Characteristic), Code format (Code Quality) [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Auto GUI (Code Quality), Black box (Testing Technique), Performance (Quality Characteristic), Code format (Test Automation)</div><div class="opt ">d. Auto GUI (Test Automation), Black box (Code Quality), Security (Testing Technique), Performance (Quality Characteristic)</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Cái này của AI nhưng ta có thể dùng foundation để phân tích nó theo nhóm, black box là test techniques, security và performance là quality characteristic của chương 2, code format là Code quality</div><h2>Cau hoi 24</h2><div class="qtext">Testing effort can depend on a number of factors, which one of the following is MOST likely to impact the amount of effort required?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. The predicted number of defects and the amount of rework required. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. The ratio of developers to testers in the project team.</div><div class="opt ">c. The planned use of a project management tool to schedule tasks.</div><div class="opt ">d. The responsibilities for testers and developers being clearly defined.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.1.4 phía dưới của các kỹ thuật estimation chúng tôi có thêm vào nội dung các factors ảnh hưởng đến việc estimate thì A là đáp án đúng.</div><h2>Cau hoi 25</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following test artifacts specifies the sequence of actions for the execution of a test?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Test script [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test procedure</div><div class="opt ">c. Test condition</div><div class="opt ">d. Test charter</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> tra glossary khái niệm về test script là ra, và các đáp án khác cũng tra glossary</div><h2>Cau hoi 26</h2><div class="qtext">In the context of testing AI-based systems or using AI for testing, which of the following represents a specialized non-functional test type unique to evaluating Machine Learning models?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Automation GUI testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Bias and fairness testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Component integration testing</div><div class="opt ">d. Performance efficiency testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Tra cứu trên mạng thì Bias và fairness là 1 kỹ thuật test cho AI tool</div><h2>Cau hoi 27</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following best describes a primary benefit of having a certain degree of independence in testing within an organization?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Independent testers can ensure that developers strictly adhere to coding standards during implementation [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Independent testers can identify different types of defects and cognitive biases that developers might overlook [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Independent testers eliminate the need for developers to perform component and integration testing</div><div class="opt ">d. Independent testers are responsible for managing the project budget and allocating testing tools.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.5 phần về independence testing, lợi ích là có 2 cái tìm ra difference và assumption thì trong này chỉ có B có ý là giúp tìm ra lỗi khác có thể bị developer bỏ qua</div><h2>Cau hoi 28</h2><div class="qtext">In a software development project utilizing a DevOps approach with a Continuous Integration / Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipeline, which of the following represents a primary responsibility of a tester to ensure continuous testing?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Write or update automated scripts for stakeholders to provide rapid quality feedback on every code commit [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Manually execute all component (unit) tests before code is integrated into the mainline branch</div><div class="opt ">c. Design complex infrastructure as code (IaC) architectures to replace traditional deployment environments</div><div class="opt ">d. Define the project scope and change management policies independent of product owners.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.1.4 phần DevOps có nhắc đến CI/CD, automation test thì vai trò của tester là tham gia vào automation test và update test scripts</div><h2>Cau hoi 29</h2><div class="qtext">Which statement best describes the key difference between a mindset for test activities and a mindset for development activities?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A tester is interested in building solutions while a developer is concerned with verifying the product b) [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. A tester is concerned with verifying the product while a developer possesses professional pessimism</div><div class="opt correct">c. A tester is concerned with finding defects while a developer is interested in designing solutions [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. A tester possesses professional pessimism while a developer is concerned with validating the product</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.5.4 bảng chia mindset của tester và developer cần nhớ rõ bảng này</div><h2>Cau hoi 30</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements regarding test techniques is CORRECT?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Exploratory testing can be used to replace formal black-box testing techniques when there is very little time available for testing [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Equivalence partitioning can only be applied during component testing and cannot be used at higher test levels.</div><div class="opt ">c. Decision table testing is an experience-based technique used primarily when system requirements are completely unwritten.</div><div class="opt ">d. Checklist-based testing is a structural test technique that requires full access to the source code repository</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.1.1 và 4.4 phần exploratory testing</div></body></html>